    "Local and cloud installers are independent artifacts. Equal or different observed digests are recorded without assuming byte identity.",
    "Formal runtime validation confirms owned processes/window response and three local GET status codes; response bodies and all formal UI flows were not inspected.",
    "GET checkers do not directly write profile data, but ordinary application startup and GET handlers may perform lifecycle migrations or catalog refreshes.",
    "Protected-data equality is the stable comparison at its stated time. Informational changes and later user edits are not silently treated as data loss or claimed unchanged.",
    "Identity checks for assets/runs/nodeRuns do not compare every private record body. Hashed manifests do not replace recovery backups.",
